    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence supports maintaining the current AMZN position at current sizing. The stock sits at a genuine inflection point: price is only 0.4% above the 50-day SMA ($144.64) and 1.2% above the lower Bollinger band, with deteriorating short-term momentum (negative MACD histogram at -1.23, RSI down from 64 to 42). However, the long-term structural case remains intact \u2014 price is 12.9% above the rising 200-day SMA, the golden cross holds, and the stock is 20% below its July 2021 high with $42.5B in nine-month operating cash flow. With no fresh catalyst on either side, neither adding aggressively nor exiting is justified. I will maintain the position and monitor the defined triggers: reduce one-third if AMZN closes below $144.64 on volume >1.0, and add toward $150-154 if it closes above $149.10 on above-average volume.\n\n**Entry Price**: 149.1\n\n**Stop Loss**: 144.64\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current weight; do not exceed neutral-to-slightly-constructive allocation until either a close above $149.10 or Q4 earnings confirm margin expansion.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
